---
title: How to Use Environment Variables
---
NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Learn how to configure and use environment variables in your TanStack Router application for API endpoints, feature flags, and build configuration across different bundlers."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"quick-start","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Quick Start"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Environment variables in TanStack Router are primarily used for client-side configuration and must follow bundler-specific naming conventions for security."}]},{"type":"code","value":"# .env\nVITE_API_URL=https://api.example.com\nVITE_ENABLE_DEVTOOLS=true","lang":"bash"},{"type":"code","value":"// Route configuration\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts')({\n  loader: async () => {\n    const apiUrl = import.meta.env.VITE_API_URL\n    const response = await fetch(`${apiUrl}/posts`)\n    return response.json()\n  },\n  component: PostsList,\n})","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"environment-variable-access-patterns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Environment Variable Access Patterns"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"vite-based-projects-most-common","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Vite-Based Projects (Most Common)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"With Vite, environment variables must be prefixed with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"VITE_"},{"type":"text","value":" to be accessible in client code:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// Route loaders\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/dashboard')({\n  loader: async () => {\n    const apiUrl = import.meta.env.VITE_API_URL        // ✅ Works\n    const apiKey = import.meta.env.VITE_PUBLIC_API_KEY // ✅ Works\n\n    // This would be undefined (security feature):\n    // const secret = import.meta.env.SECRET_KEY        // ❌ Undefined\n\n    return fetchDashboardData(apiUrl, apiKey)\n  },\n})\n\n// Components\nexport function ApiStatus() {\n  const isDev = import.meta.env.DEV           // ✅ Built-in Vite variable\n  const isProd = import.meta.env.PROD         // ✅ Built-in Vite variable\n  const mode = import.meta.env.MODE           // ✅ development/production\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      Environment: {mode}\n      {isDev && <DevToolsPanel />}\n    </div>\n  )\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"webpack-based-projects","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Webpack-Based Projects"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Configure webpack's DefinePlugin to inject environment variables. "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Note:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" Webpack doesn't support "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"import.meta.env"},{"type":"text","value":" by default, so use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"process.env"},{"type":"text","value":" patterns:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// webpack.config.js\nconst webpack = require('webpack')\n\nmodule.exports = {\n  plugins: [\n    new webpack.DefinePlugin({\n      'process.env.API_URL': JSON.stringify(process.env.API_URL),\n      'process.env.NODE_ENV': JSON.stringify(process.env.NODE_ENV),\n      'process.env.ENABLE_FEATURE': JSON.stringify(process.env.ENABLE_FEATURE),\n    }),\n  ],\n}\n\n// Usage in routes\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/api-data')({\n  loader: async () => {\n    const response = await fetch(`${process.env.API_URL}/data`)\n    return response.json()\n  },\n  component: () => {\n    const enableFeature = process.env.ENABLE_FEATURE === 'true'\n    return enableFeature ? <NewFeature /> : <OldFeature />\n  },\n})","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"rspack-based-projects","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rspack-Based Projects"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rspack uses the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"PUBLIC_"},{"type":"text","value":" prefix convention. "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Note:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"import.meta.env"},{"type":"text","value":" support depends on your Rspack configuration and runtime - you may need to configure "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"builtins.define"},{"type":"text","value":" properly:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"# .env\nPUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.example.com\nPUBLIC_FEATURE_FLAG=true","lang":"bash"},{"type":"code","value":"// Route usage\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/features')({\n  loader: async () => {\n    const apiUrl = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_API_URL\n    return fetch(`${apiUrl}/features`).then(r => r.json())\n  },\n  component: () => {\n    const enableFeature = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_FEATURE_FLAG === 'true'\n    return enableFeature ? <NewFeature /> : <OldFeature />\n  },\n})","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"esbuild-projects","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ESBuild Projects"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Configure defines manually:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// build script\nimport { build } from 'esbuild'\n\nawait build({\n  entryPoints: ['src/main.tsx'],\n  define: {\n    'process.env.NODE_ENV': '\"production\"',\n    'process.env.API_URL': `\"${process.env.API_URL}\"`,\n  },\n})","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"common-patterns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Common Patterns"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"api-configuration-in-route-loaders","children":[{"type":"text","value":"API Configuration in Route Loaders"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// src/routes/posts/index.tsx\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nconst fetchPosts = async () => {\n  const baseUrl = import.meta.env.VITE_API_URL\n  const apiKey = import.meta.env.VITE_API_KEY\n\n  const response = await fetch(`${baseUrl}/posts`, {\n    headers: {\n      'Authorization': `Bearer ${apiKey}`,\n      'Content-Type': 'application/json',\n    },\n  })\n\n  if (!response.ok) {\n    throw new Error('Failed to fetch posts')\n  }\n\n  return response.json()\n}\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/')({\n  loader: fetchPosts,\n  errorComponent: ({ error }) => (\n    <div>Error loading posts: {error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error)}</div>\n  ),\n})","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"environment-based-route-configuration","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Environment-Based Route Configuration"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// src/routes/__root.tsx\nimport { createRootRoute, Outlet } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport { TanStackRouterDevtools } from '@tanstack/react-router-devtools'\n\nexport const Route = createRootRoute({\n  component: () => (\n    <>\n      <Outlet />\n      {/* Only show devtools in development */}\n      {import.meta.env.DEV && <TanStackRouterDevtools />}\n    </>\n  ),\n})","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"feature-flags-in-routes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Feature Flags in Routes"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// src/lib/features.ts\nexport const features = {\n  enableNewDashboard: import.meta.env.VITE_ENABLE_NEW_DASHBOARD === 'true',\n  enableAnalytics: import.meta.env.VITE_ENABLE_ANALYTICS === 'true',\n  debugMode: import.meta.env.DEV,\n}\n\n// src/routes/dashboard/index.tsx\nimport { createFileRoute, redirect } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport { features } from '../../lib/features'\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/dashboard/')({\n  beforeLoad: () => {\n    // Redirect to old dashboard if new one is disabled\n    if (!features.enableNewDashboard) {\n      throw redirect({ to: '/dashboard/legacy' })\n    }\n  },\n  component: NewDashboard,\n})","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"authentication-configuration","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Authentication Configuration"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// src/lib/auth.ts\nexport const authConfig = {\n  domain: import.meta.env.VITE_AUTH0_DOMAIN,\n  clientId: import.meta.env.VITE_AUTH0_CLIENT_ID,\n  redirectUri: `${window.location.origin}/callback`,\n}\n\n// src/routes/_authenticated.tsx\nimport { createFileRoute, redirect } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport { authConfig } from '../lib/auth'\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/_authenticated')({\n  beforeLoad: async ({ location }) => {\n    const isAuthenticated = await checkAuthStatus()\n\n    if (!isAuthenticated) {\n      // Redirect to auth provider\n      const authUrl = `https://${authConfig.domain}/authorize?client_id=${authConfig.clientId}&redirect_uri=${authConfig.redirectUri}`\n      window.location.href = authUrl\n      return\n    }\n  },\n})","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"search-params-with-environment-config","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Search Params with Environment Config"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// src/routes/search.tsx\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nconst searchSchema = z.object({\n  q: z.string().optional(),\n  category: z.string().optional(),\n})\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/search')({\n  validateSearch: searchSchema,\n  loader: async ({ search }) => {\n    const apiUrl = import.meta.env.VITE_SEARCH_API_URL\n    const params = new URLSearchParams({\n      q: search.q || '',\n      category: search.category || 'all',\n      api_key: import.meta.env.VITE_SEARCH_API_KEY,\n    })\n\n    const response = await fetch(`${apiUrl}/search?${params}`)\n    return response.json()\n  },\n})","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"environment-file-setup","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Environment File Setup"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"file-hierarchy-vite","children":[{"type":"text","value":"File Hierarchy (Vite)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Vite loads environment files in this order:"}]},{"type":"code","value":".env.local          # Local overrides (add to .gitignore)\n.env.production     # Production-specific\n.env.development    # Development-specific\n.env                # Default (commit to git)"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"example-configuration","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example Configuration"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":".env"}]},{"type":"text","value":" (committed to repository):"}]},{"type":"code","value":"# API Configuration\nVITE_API_URL=https://api.example.com\nVITE_API_VERSION=v1\n\n# Feature Flags\nVITE_ENABLE_NEW_UI=false\nVITE_ENABLE_ANALYTICS=true\n\n# Auth Configuration (public keys only)\nVITE_AUTH0_DOMAIN=your-domain.auth0.com\nVITE_AUTH0_CLIENT_ID=your-client-id\n\n# Build Configuration\nVITE_APP_NAME=TanStack Router App\nVITE_APP_VERSION=1.0.0","lang":"bash"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":".env.local"}]},{"type":"text","value":" (add to .gitignore):"}]},{"type":"code","value":"# Development overrides\nVITE_API_URL=http://localhost:3001\nVITE_ENABLE_NEW_UI=true\nVITE_DEBUG_MODE=true","lang":"bash"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":".env.production"}]},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"# Production-specific\nVITE_API_URL=https://api.prod.example.com\nVITE_ENABLE_ANALYTICS=true\nVITE_ENABLE_NEW_UI=true","lang":"bash"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-safety","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Safety"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"vite-typescript-declarations","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Vite TypeScript Declarations"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Create "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"src/vite-env.d.ts"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"/// <reference types=\"vite/client\" />\n\ninterface ImportMetaEnv {\n  // API Configuration\n  readonly VITE_API_URL: string\n  readonly VITE_API_VERSION: string\n  readonly VITE_API_KEY?: string\n\n  // Feature Flags\n  readonly VITE_ENABLE_NEW_UI: string\n  readonly VITE_ENABLE_ANALYTICS: string\n  readonly VITE_DEBUG_MODE?: string\n\n  // Authentication\n  readonly VITE_AUTH0_DOMAIN: string\n  readonly VITE_AUTH0_CLIENT_ID: string\n\n  // App Configuration\n  readonly VITE_APP_NAME: string\n  readonly VITE_APP_VERSION: string\n}\n\ninterface ImportMeta {\n  readonly env: ImportMetaEnv\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"runtime-validation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Runtime Validation"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use Zod to validate environment variables at startup with fallbacks and optional values:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// src/config/env.ts\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nconst envSchema = z.object({\n  // Required variables\n  VITE_API_URL: z.string().url(),\n  VITE_AUTH0_DOMAIN: z.string(),\n  VITE_AUTH0_CLIENT_ID: z.string(),\n  VITE_APP_NAME: z.string(),\n\n  // Optional with defaults\n  VITE_API_VERSION: z.string().default('v1'),\n  VITE_ENABLE_NEW_UI: z.string().default('false'),\n  VITE_ENABLE_ANALYTICS: z.string().default('true'),\n\n  // Optional variables\n  VITE_DEBUG_MODE: z.string().optional(),\n  VITE_SENTRY_DSN: z.string().optional(),\n})\n\n// Validate at app startup with fallbacks\nexport const env = envSchema.parse({\n  ...import.meta.env,\n  // Provide fallbacks for missing optional values\n  VITE_API_VERSION: import.meta.env.VITE_API_VERSION || 'v1',\n  VITE_ENABLE_NEW_UI: import.meta.env.VITE_ENABLE_NEW_UI || 'false',\n  VITE_ENABLE_ANALYTICS: import.meta.env.VITE_ENABLE_ANALYTICS || 'true',\n})\n\n// Typed helper functions\nexport const isFeatureEnabled = (flag: keyof typeof env) => {\n  return env[flag] === 'true'\n}\n\n// Type-safe boolean conversion\nexport const getBooleanEnv = (\n  value: string | undefined,\n  defaultValue = false,\n): boolean => {\n  if (value === undefined) return defaultValue\n  return value === 'true'\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"usage-with-type-safety","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Usage with Type Safety"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// src/routes/api-data.tsx\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport { env, isFeatureEnabled } from '../config/env'\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/api-data')({\n  loader: async () => {\n    // TypeScript knows these are strings and exist\n    const response = await fetch(`${env.VITE_API_URL}/${env.VITE_API_VERSION}/data`)\n    return response.json()\n  },\n  component: () => {\n    return (\n      <div>\n        <h1>{env.VITE_APP_NAME}</h1>\n        {isFeatureEnabled('VITE_ENABLE_NEW_UI') && <NewUIComponent />}\n      </div>\n    )\n  },\n})","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"bundler-specific-configuration","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Bundler-Specific Configuration"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"vite-configuration","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Vite Configuration"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// vite.config.ts\nimport { defineConfig } from 'vite'\nimport react from '@vitejs/plugin-react'\nimport { tanstackRouter } from '@tanstack/router-plugin/vite'\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  plugins: [\n    react(),\n    // tanstackRouter generates route tree and enables file-based routing\n    tanstackRouter(),\n  ],\n  // Environment variables are handled automatically\n  // Custom environment variable handling:\n  define: {\n    // Global constants (these become available as global variables)\n    __APP_VERSION__: JSON.stringify(process.env.npm_package_version),\n  },\n})","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"webpack-configuration","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Webpack Configuration"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// webpack.config.js\nconst { TanStackRouterWebpack } = require('@tanstack/router-webpack-plugin')\nconst webpack = require('webpack')\n\nmodule.exports = {\n  plugins: [\n    // TanStackRouterWebpack generates route tree and enables file-based routing\n    new TanStackRouterWebpack(),\n    new webpack.DefinePlugin({\n      // Inject environment variables (use process.env for Webpack)\n      'process.env.API_URL': JSON.stringify(process.env.API_URL),\n      'process.env.NODE_ENV': JSON.stringify(process.env.NODE_ENV),\n      'process.env.ENABLE_FEATURE': JSON.stringify(process.env.ENABLE_FEATURE),\n    }),\n  ],\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"rspack-configuration","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rspack Configuration"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// rspack.config.js\nconst { TanStackRouterRspack } = require('@tanstack/router-rspack-plugin')\n\nmodule.exports = {\n  plugins: [\n    // TanStackRouterRspack generates route tree and enables file-based routing\n    new TanStackRouterRspack(),\n  ],\n  // Rspack automatically handles PUBLIC_ prefixed variables for import.meta.env\n  // Custom handling for additional variables:\n  builtins: {\n    define: {\n      // Define additional variables (these become global replacements)\n      'process.env.API_URL': JSON.stringify(process.env.PUBLIC_API_URL),\n      __BUILD_TIME__: JSON.stringify(new Date().toISOString()),\n    },\n  },\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"production-checklist","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Production Checklist"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"All client-exposed variables use appropriate prefix ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"VITE_"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"PUBLIC_"},{"type":"text","value":", etc.)"}]}],"checked":false},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No sensitive data (API secrets, private keys) in environment variables"}]}],"checked":false},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":".env.local"},{"type":"text","value":" is in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".gitignore"}]}],"checked":false},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Production environment variables are configured on hosting platform"}]}],"checked":false},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Required environment variables are validated at build time"}]}],"checked":false},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TypeScript declarations are up to date"}]}],"checked":false},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Feature flags are properly configured for production"}]}],"checked":false},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"API URLs point to production endpoints"}]}],"checked":false}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"common-problems","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Common Problems"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"environment-variable-is-undefined","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Environment Variable is Undefined"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Problem"}]},{"type":"text","value":": "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"import.meta.env.MY_VARIABLE"},{"type":"text","value":" returns "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"undefined"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Solutions"}]},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Add correct prefix"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"VITE_"},{"type":"text","value":" for Vite, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"PUBLIC_"},{"type":"text","value":" for Rspack.\nVite's default prefix may be changed in the config:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// vite.config.ts\nexport const config = {\n  // ...rest of your config\n  envPrefix: 'MYPREFIX_', // this means `MYPREFIX_MY_VARIABLE` is the new correct way\n}","lang":"ts"}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Restart development server"}]},{"type":"text","value":" after adding new variables"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Check file location"}]},{"type":"text","value":": "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".env"},{"type":"text","value":" file must be in project root"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Verify bundler configuration"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Ensure variables are properly injected"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Verify variable"}]},{"type":"text","value":":"}]}]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In dev"}]},{"type":"text","value":": is in correct "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".env"},{"type":"text","value":" file or environment"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For prod"}]},{"type":"text","value":": is in correct "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".env"},{"type":"text","value":" file or current environment "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"at bundle time"}]}]},{"type":"text","value":". That's right, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"VITE_"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"PUBLIC_"},{"type":"text","value":"-prefixed variables are replaced in a macro-like fashion at bundle time, and will "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"never"}]},{"type":"text","value":" be read at runtime on your server. This is a common mistake, so make sure this is not your case."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"# ❌ Won't work (no prefix)\nAPI_KEY=abc123\n\n# ✅ Works with Vite\nVITE_API_KEY=abc123\n\n# ✅ Works with Rspack\nPUBLIC_API_KEY=abc123\n\n# ❌ Won't bundle the variable (assuming it is not set in the environment of the build)\nnpm run build\n\n# ✅ Works with Vite and will bundle the variable for production\nVITE_API_KEY=abc123 npm run build\n\n# ✅ Works with Rspack and will bundle the variable for production\nPUBLIC_API_KEY=abc123 npm run build","lang":"bash"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"runtime-client-environment-variables-at-runtime-in-production","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Runtime Client Environment Variables at Runtime in Production"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Problem"}]},{"type":"text","value":": If "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"VITE_"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"PUBLIC_"},{"type":"text","value":" variables are replaced at bundle time only, how to make runtime variables available on the client ?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Solutions"}]},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass variables from the server down to the client:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Add your variable to the correct "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"env."},{"type":"text","value":" file"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Create an endpoint on your server to read the value from the client"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You may use your prefered backend framework/libray, but here it is using Tanstack Start server functions:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const getRuntimeVar = createServerFn({ method: 'GET' }).handler(() => {\n  return process.env.MY_RUNTIME_VAR // notice `process.env` on the server, and no `VITE_`/`PUBLIC_` prefix\n})\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/')({\n  loader: async () => {\n    const foo = await getRuntimeVar()\n    return { foo }\n  },\n  component: RouteComponent,\n})\n\nfunction RouteComponent() {\n  const { foo } = Route.useLoaderData()\n  // ... use your variable however you want\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"variable-not-updating","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Variable Not Updating"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Problem"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Environment variable changes aren't reflected in app"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Solutions"}]},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Restart development server"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Required for new variables"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Check file hierarchy"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".env.local"},{"type":"text","value":" overrides "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".env"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Clear browser cache"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Hard refresh (Ctrl+Shift+R)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Verify correct file"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Make sure you're editing the right "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".env"},{"type":"text","value":" file"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"typescript-errors","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TypeScript Errors"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Problem"}]},{"type":"text","value":": "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Property 'VITE_MY_VAR' does not exist on type 'ImportMetaEnv'"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Solution"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Add declaration to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"src/vite-env.d.ts"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"interface ImportMetaEnv {\n  readonly VITE_MY_VAR: string\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"build-errors","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Build Errors"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Problem"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Missing environment variables during build"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Solutions"}]},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Configure CI/CD"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Set variables in build environment"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Add validation"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Check required variables at build time"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use .env files"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Ensure production "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".env"},{"type":"text","value":" files exist"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Check bundler config"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Verify environment variable injection"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"security-issues","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Security Issues"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Problem"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Accidentally exposing sensitive data"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Solutions"}]},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Never use secrets in client variables"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - They're visible in browser"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use server-side proxies"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for sensitive API calls"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Audit bundle"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Check built files for leaked secrets"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Follow naming conventions"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Only prefixed variables are exposed"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"runtime-vs-build-time-confusion","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Runtime vs Build-time Confusion"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Problem"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Variables not available at runtime"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Solutions"}]},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Understand static replacement"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Variables are replaced at build time"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use server-side for dynamic values"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Use APIs for runtime configuration"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Validate at startup"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Check all required variables exist"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"environment-variables-are-always-strings","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Environment Variables are Always Strings"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Problem"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Unexpected behavior when comparing boolean or numeric values"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Solutions"}]},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Always compare as strings"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"=== 'true'"},{"type":"text","value":" not "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"=== true"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Convert explicitly"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"parseInt()"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"parseFloat()"},{"type":"text","value":", or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Boolean()"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use helper functions"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Create typed conversion utilities"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// ❌ Won't work as expected\nconst isEnabled = import.meta.env.VITE_FEATURE_ENABLED // This is a string!\nif (isEnabled) {\n  /* Always true if variable exists */\n}\n\n// ✅ Correct string comparison\nconst isEnabled = import.meta.env.VITE_FEATURE_ENABLED === 'true'\n\n// ✅ Safe numeric conversion\nconst port = parseInt(import.meta.env.VITE_PORT || '3000', 10)\n\n// ✅ Helper function approach\nconst getBooleanEnv = (value: string | undefined, defaultValue = false) => {\n  if (value === undefined) return defaultValue\n  return value.toLowerCase() === 'true'\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"common-next-steps","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Common Next Steps"}]},{"type":"html","value":"<!-- [Set Up Authentication](./setup-authentication.md) - Configure auth providers with environment variables -->"},{"type":"html","value":"<!-- [Deploy to Production](./deploy-to-production.md) - Set up production environment variables -->"},{"type":"html","value":"<!-- [Set Up API Integration](./setup-api-integration.md) - Configure API endpoints and keys -->"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"related-resources","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Related Resources"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../routing/file-based-routing.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Router File-Based Routing"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Learn about route configuration"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://vitejs.dev/guide/env-and-mode.html","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Vite Environment Variables"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Official Vite documentation"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://webpack.js.org/plugins/define-plugin/","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Webpack DefinePlugin"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Webpack environment configuration"}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"quick-start","text":"Quick Start","level":2},{"id":"environment-variable-access-patterns","text":"Environment Variable Access Patterns","level":2},{"id":"vite-based-projects-most-common","text":"Vite-Based Projects (Most Common)","level":3},{"id":"webpack-based-projects","text":"Webpack-Based Projects","level":3},{"id":"rspack-based-projects","text":"Rspack-Based Projects","level":3},{"id":"esbuild-projects","text":"ESBuild Projects","level":3},{"id":"common-patterns","text":"Common Patterns","level":2},{"id":"api-configuration-in-route-loaders","text":"API Configuration in Route Loaders","level":3},{"id":"environment-based-route-configuration","text":"Environment-Based Route Configuration","level":3},{"id":"feature-flags-in-routes","text":"Feature Flags in Routes","level":3},{"id":"authentication-configuration","text":"Authentication Configuration","level":3},{"id":"search-params-with-environment-config","text":"Search Params with Environment Config","level":3},{"id":"environment-file-setup","text":"Environment File Setup","level":2},{"id":"file-hierarchy-vite","text":"File Hierarchy (Vite)","level":3},{"id":"example-configuration","text":"Example Configuration","level":3},{"id":"type-safety","text":"Type Safety","level":2},{"id":"vite-typescript-declarations","text":"Vite TypeScript Declarations","level":3},{"id":"runtime-validation","text":"Runtime Validation","level":3},{"id":"usage-with-type-safety","text":"Usage with Type Safety","level":3},{"id":"bundler-specific-configuration","text":"Bundler-Specific Configuration","level":2},{"id":"vite-configuration","text":"Vite Configuration","level":3},{"id":"webpack-configuration","text":"Webpack Configuration","level":3},{"id":"rspack-configuration","text":"Rspack Configuration","level":3},{"id":"production-checklist","text":"Production Checklist","level":2},{"id":"common-problems","text":"Common Problems","level":2},{"id":"environment-variable-is-undefined","text":"Environment Variable is Undefined","level":3},{"id":"runtime-client-environment-variables-at-runtime-in-production","text":"Runtime Client Environment Variables at Runtime in Production","level":3},{"id":"variable-not-updating","text":"Variable Not Updating","level":3},{"id":"typescript-errors","text":"TypeScript Errors","level":3},{"id":"build-errors","text":"Build Errors","level":3},{"id":"security-issues","text":"Security Issues","level":3},{"id":"runtime-vs-build-time-confusion","text":"Runtime vs Build-time Confusion","level":3},{"id":"environment-variables-are-always-strings","text":"Environment Variables are Always Strings","level":3},{"id":"common-next-steps","text":"Common Next Steps","level":2},{"id":"related-resources","text":"Related Resources","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nLearn how to configure and use environment variables in your TanStack Router application for API endpoints, feature flags, and build configuration across different bundlers.\n\n## Quick Start\n\nEnvironment variables in TanStack Router are primarily used for client-side configuration and must follow bundler-specific naming conventions for security.\n\n```bash\n# .env\nVITE_API_URL=https://api.example.com\nVITE_ENABLE_DEVTOOLS=true\n```\n\n```typescript\n// Route configuration\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts')({\n  loader: async () => {\n    const apiUrl = import.meta.env.VITE_API_URL\n    const response = await fetch(`${apiUrl}/posts`)\n    return response.json()\n  },\n  component: PostsList,\n})\n```\n\n## Environment Variable Access Patterns\n\n### Vite-Based Projects (Most Common)\n\nWith Vite, environment variables must be prefixed with `VITE_` to be accessible in client code:\n\n```typescript\n// Route loaders\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/dashboard')({\n  loader: async () => {\n    const apiUrl = import.meta.env.VITE_API_URL        // ✅ Works\n    const apiKey = import.meta.env.VITE_PUBLIC_API_KEY // ✅ Works\n\n    // This would be undefined (security feature):\n    // const secret = import.meta.env.SECRET_KEY        // ❌ Undefined\n\n    return fetchDashboardData(apiUrl, apiKey)\n  },\n})\n\n// Components\nexport function ApiStatus() {\n  const isDev = import.meta.env.DEV           // ✅ Built-in Vite variable\n  const isProd = import.meta.env.PROD         // ✅ Built-in Vite variable\n  const mode = import.meta.env.MODE           // ✅ development/production\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      Environment: {mode}\n      {isDev && <DevToolsPanel />}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n### Webpack-Based Projects\n\nConfigure webpack's DefinePlugin to inject environment variables. **Note:** Webpack doesn't support `import.meta.env` by default, so use `process.env` patterns:\n\n```typescript\n// webpack.config.js\nconst webpack = require('webpack')\n\nmodule.exports = {\n  plugins: [\n    new webpack.DefinePlugin({\n      'process.env.API_URL': JSON.stringify(process.env.API_URL),\n      'process.env.NODE_ENV': JSON.stringify(process.env.NODE_ENV),\n      'process.env.ENABLE_FEATURE': JSON.stringify(process.env.ENABLE_FEATURE),\n    }),\n  ],\n}\n\n// Usage in routes\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/api-data')({\n  loader: async () => {\n    const response = await fetch(`${process.env.API_URL}/data`)\n    return response.json()\n  },\n  component: () => {\n    const enableFeature = process.env.ENABLE_FEATURE === 'true'\n    return enableFeature ? <NewFeature /> : <OldFeature />\n  },\n})\n```\n\n### Rspack-Based Projects\n\nRspack uses the `PUBLIC_` prefix convention. **Note:** `import.meta.env` support depends on your Rspack configuration and runtime - you may need to configure `builtins.define` properly:\n\n```bash\n# .env\nPUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.example.com\nPUBLIC_FEATURE_FLAG=true\n```\n\n```typescript\n// Route usage\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/features')({\n  loader: async () => {\n    const apiUrl = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_API_URL\n    return fetch(`${apiUrl}/features`).then(r => r.json())\n  },\n  component: () => {\n    const enableFeature = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_FEATURE_FLAG === 'true'\n    return enableFeature ? <NewFeature /> : <OldFeature />\n  },\n})\n```\n\n### ESBuild Projects\n\nConfigure defines manually:\n\n```typescript\n// build script\nimport { build } from 'esbuild'\n\nawait build({\n  entryPoints: ['src/main.tsx'],\n  define: {\n    'process.env.NODE_ENV': '\"production\"',\n    'process.env.API_URL': `\"${process.env.API_URL}\"`,\n  },\n})\n```\n\n## Common Patterns\n\n### API Configuration in Route Loaders\n\n```typescript\n// src/routes/posts/index.tsx\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nconst fetchPosts = async () => {\n  const baseUrl = import.meta.env.VITE_API_URL\n  const apiKey = import.meta.env.VITE_API_KEY\n\n  const response = await fetch(`${baseUrl}/posts`, {\n    headers: {\n      'Authorization': `Bearer ${apiKey}`,\n      'Content-Type': 'application/json',\n    },\n  })\n\n  if (!response.ok) {\n    throw new Error('Failed to fetch posts')\n  }\n\n  return response.json()\n}\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/')({\n  loader: fetchPosts,\n  errorComponent: ({ error }) => (\n    <div>Error loading posts: {error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error)}</div>\n  ),\n})\n```\n\n### Environment-Based Route Configuration\n\n```typescript\n// src/routes/__root.tsx\nimport { createRootRoute, Outlet } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport { TanStackRouterDevtools } from '@tanstack/react-router-devtools'\n\nexport const Route = createRootRoute({\n  component: () => (\n    <>\n      <Outlet />\n      {/* Only show devtools in development */}\n      {import.meta.env.DEV && <TanStackRouterDevtools />}\n    </>\n  ),\n})\n```\n\n### Feature Flags in Routes\n\n```typescript\n// src/lib/features.ts\nexport const features = {\n  enableNewDashboard: import.meta.env.VITE_ENABLE_NEW_DASHBOARD === 'true',\n  enableAnalytics: import.meta.env.VITE_ENABLE_ANALYTICS === 'true',\n  debugMode: import.meta.env.DEV,\n}\n\n// src/routes/dashboard/index.tsx\nimport { createFileRoute, redirect } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport { features } from '../../lib/features'\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/dashboard/')({\n  beforeLoad: () => {\n    // Redirect to old dashboard if new one is disabled\n    if (!features.enableNewDashboard) {\n      throw redirect({ to: '/dashboard/legacy' })\n    }\n  },\n  component: NewDashboard,\n})\n```\n\n### Authentication Configuration\n\n```typescript\n// src/lib/auth.ts\nexport const authConfig = {\n  domain: import.meta.env.VITE_AUTH0_DOMAIN,\n  clientId: import.meta.env.VITE_AUTH0_CLIENT_ID,\n  redirectUri: `${window.location.origin}/callback`,\n}\n\n// src/routes/_authenticated.tsx\nimport { createFileRoute, redirect } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport { authConfig } from '../lib/auth'\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/_authenticated')({\n  beforeLoad: async ({ location }) => {\n    const isAuthenticated = await checkAuthStatus()\n\n    if (!isAuthenticated) {\n      // Redirect to auth provider\n      const authUrl = `https://${authConfig.domain}/authorize?client_id=${authConfig.clientId}&redirect_uri=${authConfig.redirectUri}`\n      window.location.href = authUrl\n      return\n    }\n  },\n})\n```\n\n### Search Params with Environment Config\n\n```typescript\n// src/routes/search.tsx\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nconst searchSchema = z.object({\n  q: z.string().optional(),\n  category: z.string().optional(),\n})\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/search')({\n  validateSearch: searchSchema,\n  loader: async ({ search }) => {\n    const apiUrl = import.meta.env.VITE_SEARCH_API_URL\n    const params = new URLSearchParams({\n      q: search.q || '',\n      category: search.category || 'all',\n      api_key: import.meta.env.VITE_SEARCH_API_KEY,\n    })\n\n    const response = await fetch(`${apiUrl}/search?${params}`)\n    return response.json()\n  },\n})\n```\n\n## Environment File Setup\n\n### File Hierarchy (Vite)\n\nVite loads environment files in this order:\n\n```\n.env.local          # Local overrides (add to .gitignore)\n.env.production     # Production-specific\n.env.development    # Development-specific\n.env                # Default (commit to git)\n```\n\n### Example Configuration\n\n**.env** (committed to repository):\n\n```bash\n# API Configuration\nVITE_API_URL=https://api.example.com\nVITE_API_VERSION=v1\n\n# Feature Flags\nVITE_ENABLE_NEW_UI=false\nVITE_ENABLE_ANALYTICS=true\n\n# Auth Configuration (public keys only)\nVITE_AUTH0_DOMAIN=your-domain.auth0.com\nVITE_AUTH0_CLIENT_ID=your-client-id\n\n# Build Configuration\nVITE_APP_NAME=TanStack Router App\nVITE_APP_VERSION=1.0.0\n```\n\n**.env.local** (add to .gitignore):\n\n```bash\n# Development overrides\nVITE_API_URL=http://localhost:3001\nVITE_ENABLE_NEW_UI=true\nVITE_DEBUG_MODE=true\n```\n\n**.env.production**:\n\n```bash\n# Production-specific\nVITE_API_URL=https://api.prod.example.com\nVITE_ENABLE_ANALYTICS=true\nVITE_ENABLE_NEW_UI=true\n```\n\n## Type Safety\n\n### Vite TypeScript Declarations\n\nCreate `src/vite-env.d.ts`:\n\n```typescript\n/// <reference types=\"vite/client\" />\n\ninterface ImportMetaEnv {\n  // API Configuration\n  readonly VITE_API_URL: string\n  readonly VITE_API_VERSION: string\n  readonly VITE_API_KEY?: string\n\n  // Feature Flags\n  readonly VITE_ENABLE_NEW_UI: string\n  readonly VITE_ENABLE_ANALYTICS: string\n  readonly VITE_DEBUG_MODE?: string\n\n  // Authentication\n  readonly VITE_AUTH0_DOMAIN: string\n  readonly VITE_AUTH0_CLIENT_ID: string\n\n  // App Configuration\n  readonly VITE_APP_NAME: string\n  readonly VITE_APP_VERSION: string\n}\n\ninterface ImportMeta {\n  readonly env: ImportMetaEnv\n}\n```\n\n### Runtime Validation\n\nUse Zod to validate environment variables at startup with fallbacks and optional values:\n\n```typescript\n// src/config/env.ts\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nconst envSchema = z.object({\n  // Required variables\n  VITE_API_URL: z.string().url(),\n  VITE_AUTH0_DOMAIN: z.string(),\n  VITE_AUTH0_CLIENT_ID: z.string(),\n  VITE_APP_NAME: z.string(),\n\n  // Optional with defaults\n  VITE_API_VERSION: z.string().default('v1'),\n  VITE_ENABLE_NEW_UI: z.string().default('false'),\n  VITE_ENABLE_ANALYTICS: z.string().default('true'),\n\n  // Optional variables\n  VITE_DEBUG_MODE: z.string().optional(),\n  VITE_SENTRY_DSN: z.string().optional(),\n})\n\n// Validate at app startup with fallbacks\nexport const env = envSchema.parse({\n  ...import.meta.env,\n  // Provide fallbacks for missing optional values\n  VITE_API_VERSION: import.meta.env.VITE_API_VERSION || 'v1',\n  VITE_ENABLE_NEW_UI: import.meta.env.VITE_ENABLE_NEW_UI || 'false',\n  VITE_ENABLE_ANALYTICS: import.meta.env.VITE_ENABLE_ANALYTICS || 'true',\n})\n\n// Typed helper functions\nexport const isFeatureEnabled = (flag: keyof typeof env) => {\n  return env[flag] === 'true'\n}\n\n// Type-safe boolean conversion\nexport const getBooleanEnv = (\n  value: string | undefined,\n  defaultValue = false,\n): boolean => {\n  if (value === undefined) return defaultValue\n  return value === 'true'\n}\n```\n\n### Usage with Type Safety\n\n```typescript\n// src/routes/api-data.tsx\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport { env, isFeatureEnabled } from '../config/env'\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/api-data')({\n  loader: async () => {\n    // TypeScript knows these are strings and exist\n    const response = await fetch(`${env.VITE_API_URL}/${env.VITE_API_VERSION}/data`)\n    return response.json()\n  },\n  component: () => {\n    return (\n      <div>\n        <h1>{env.VITE_APP_NAME}</h1>\n        {isFeatureEnabled('VITE_ENABLE_NEW_UI') && <NewUIComponent />}\n      </div>\n    )\n  },\n})\n```\n\n## Bundler-Specific Configuration\n\n### Vite Configuration\n\n```typescript\n// vite.config.ts\nimport { defineConfig } from 'vite'\nimport react from '@vitejs/plugin-react'\nimport { tanstackRouter } from '@tanstack/router-plugin/vite'\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  plugins: [\n    react(),\n    // tanstackRouter generates route tree and enables file-based routing\n    tanstackRouter(),\n  ],\n  // Environment variables are handled automatically\n  // Custom environment variable handling:\n  define: {\n    // Global constants (these become available as global variables)\n    __APP_VERSION__: JSON.stringify(process.env.npm_package_version),\n  },\n})\n```\n\n### Webpack Configuration\n\n```typescript\n// webpack.config.js\nconst { TanStackRouterWebpack } = require('@tanstack/router-webpack-plugin')\nconst webpack = require('webpack')\n\nmodule.exports = {\n  plugins: [\n    // TanStackRouterWebpack generates route tree and enables file-based routing\n    new TanStackRouterWebpack(),\n    new webpack.DefinePlugin({\n      // Inject environment variables (use process.env for Webpack)\n      'process.env.API_URL': JSON.stringify(process.env.API_URL),\n      'process.env.NODE_ENV': JSON.stringify(process.env.NODE_ENV),\n      'process.env.ENABLE_FEATURE': JSON.stringify(process.env.ENABLE_FEATURE),\n    }),\n  ],\n}\n```\n\n### Rspack Configuration\n\n```typescript\n// rspack.config.js\nconst { TanStackRouterRspack } = require('@tanstack/router-rspack-plugin')\n\nmodule.exports = {\n  plugins: [\n    // TanStackRouterRspack generates route tree and enables file-based routing\n    new TanStackRouterRspack(),\n  ],\n  // Rspack automatically handles PUBLIC_ prefixed variables for import.meta.env\n  // Custom handling for additional variables:\n  builtins: {\n    define: {\n      // Define additional variables (these become global replacements)\n      'process.env.API_URL': JSON.stringify(process.env.PUBLIC_API_URL),\n      __BUILD_TIME__: JSON.stringify(new Date().toISOString()),\n    },\n  },\n}\n```\n\n## Production Checklist\n\n- [ ] All client-exposed variables use appropriate prefix (`VITE_`, `PUBLIC_`, etc.)\n- [ ] No sensitive data (API secrets, private keys) in environment variables\n- [ ] `.env.local` is in `.gitignore`\n- [ ] Production environment variables are configured on hosting platform\n- [ ] Required environment variables are validated at build time\n- [ ] TypeScript declarations are up to date\n- [ ] Feature flags are properly configured for production\n- [ ] API URLs point to production endpoints\n\n## Common Problems\n\n### Environment Variable is Undefined\n\n**Problem**: `import.meta.env.MY_VARIABLE` returns `undefined`\n\n**Solutions**:\n\n1. **Add correct prefix**: Use `VITE_` for Vite, `PUBLIC_` for Rspack.\n   Vite's default prefix may be changed in the config:\n   ```ts\n   // vite.config.ts\n   export const config = {\n     // ...rest of your config\n     envPrefix: 'MYPREFIX_', // this means `MYPREFIX_MY_VARIABLE` is the new correct way\n   }\n   ```\n2. **Restart development server** after adding new variables\n3. **Check file location**: `.env` file must be in project root\n4. **Verify bundler configuration**: Ensure variables are properly injected\n5. **Verify variable**:\n\n- **In dev**: is in correct `.env` file or environment\n- **For prod**: is in correct `.env` file or current environment **_at bundle time_**. That's right, `VITE_`/`PUBLIC_`-prefixed variables are replaced in a macro-like fashion at bundle time, and will _never_ be read at runtime on your server. This is a common mistake, so make sure this is not your case.\n\n**Example**:\n\n```bash\n# ❌ Won't work (no prefix)\nAPI_KEY=abc123\n\n# ✅ Works with Vite\nVITE_API_KEY=abc123\n\n# ✅ Works with Rspack\nPUBLIC_API_KEY=abc123\n\n# ❌ Won't bundle the variable (assuming it is not set in the environment of the build)\nnpm run build\n\n# ✅ Works with Vite and will bundle the variable for production\nVITE_API_KEY=abc123 npm run build\n\n# ✅ Works with Rspack and will bundle the variable for production\nPUBLIC_API_KEY=abc123 npm run build\n```\n\n### Runtime Client Environment Variables at Runtime in Production\n\n**Problem**: If `VITE_`/`PUBLIC_` variables are replaced at bundle time only, how to make runtime variables available on the client ?\n\n**Solutions**:\n\nPass variables from the server down to the client:\n\n1. Add your variable to the correct `env.` file\n2. Create an endpoint on your server to read the value from the client\n\n**Example**:\n\nYou may use your prefered backend framework/libray, but here it is using Tanstack Start server functions:\n\n```tsx\nconst getRuntimeVar = createServerFn({ method: 'GET' }).handler(() => {\n  return process.env.MY_RUNTIME_VAR // notice `process.env` on the server, and no `VITE_`/`PUBLIC_` prefix\n})\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/')({\n  loader: async () => {\n    const foo = await getRuntimeVar()\n    return { foo }\n  },\n  component: RouteComponent,\n})\n\nfunction RouteComponent() {\n  const { foo } = Route.useLoaderData()\n  // ... use your variable however you want\n}\n```\n\n### Variable Not Updating\n\n**Problem**: Environment variable changes aren't reflected in app\n\n**Solutions**:\n\n1. **Restart development server** - Required for new variables\n2. **Check file hierarchy** - `.env.local` overrides `.env`\n3. **Clear browser cache** - Hard refresh (Ctrl+Shift+R)\n4. **Verify correct file** - Make sure you're editing the right `.env` file\n\n### TypeScript Errors\n\n**Problem**: `Property 'VITE_MY_VAR' does not exist on type 'ImportMetaEnv'`\n\n**Solution**: Add declaration to `src/vite-env.d.ts`:\n\n```typescript\ninterface ImportMetaEnv {\n  readonly VITE_MY_VAR: string\n}\n```\n\n### Build Errors\n\n**Problem**: Missing environment variables during build\n\n**Solutions**:\n\n1. **Configure CI/CD**: Set variables in build environment\n2. **Add validation**: Check required variables at build time\n3. **Use .env files**: Ensure production `.env` files exist\n4. **Check bundler config**: Verify environment variable injection\n\n### Security Issues\n\n**Problem**: Accidentally exposing sensitive data\n\n**Solutions**:\n\n1. **Never use secrets in client variables** - They're visible in browser\n2. **Use server-side proxies** for sensitive API calls\n3. **Audit bundle** - Check built files for leaked secrets\n4. **Follow naming conventions** - Only prefixed variables are exposed\n\n### Runtime vs Build-time Confusion\n\n**Problem**: Variables not available at runtime\n\n**Solutions**:\n\n1. **Understand static replacement** - Variables are replaced at build time\n2. **Use server-side for dynamic values** - Use APIs for runtime configuration\n3. **Validate at startup** - Check all required variables exist\n\n### Environment Variables are Always Strings\n\n**Problem**: Unexpected behavior when comparing boolean or numeric values\n\n**Solutions**:\n\n1. **Always compare as strings**: Use `=== 'true'` not `=== true`\n2. **Convert explicitly**: Use `parseInt()`, `parseFloat()`, or `Boolean()`\n3. **Use helper functions**: Create typed conversion utilities\n\n**Example**:\n\n```typescript\n// ❌ Won't work as expected\nconst isEnabled = import.meta.env.VITE_FEATURE_ENABLED // This is a string!\nif (isEnabled) {\n  /* Always true if variable exists */\n}\n\n// ✅ Correct string comparison\nconst isEnabled = import.meta.env.VITE_FEATURE_ENABLED === 'true'\n\n// ✅ Safe numeric conversion\nconst port = parseInt(import.meta.env.VITE_PORT || '3000', 10)\n\n// ✅ Helper function approach\nconst getBooleanEnv = (value: string | undefined, defaultValue = false) => {\n  if (value === undefined) return defaultValue\n  return value.toLowerCase() === 'true'\n}\n```\n\n## Common Next Steps\n\n<!-- [Set Up Authentication](./setup-authentication.md) - Configure auth providers with environment variables -->\n<!-- [Deploy to Production](./deploy-to-production.md) - Set up production environment variables -->\n<!-- [Set Up API Integration](./setup-api-integration.md) - Configure API endpoints and keys -->\n\n## Related Resources\n\n- [TanStack Router File-Based Routing](../routing/file-based-routing.md) - Learn about route configuration\n- [Vite Environment Variables](https://vitejs.dev/guide/env-and-mode.html) - Official Vite documentation\n- [Webpack DefinePlugin](https://webpack.js.org/plugins/define-plugin/) - Webpack environment configuration\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: How to Use Environment Variables\n---\n\nLearn how to configure and use environment variables in your TanStack Router application for API endpoints, feature flags, and build configuration across different bundlers.\n\n## Quick Start\n\nEnvironment variables in TanStack Router are primarily used for client-side configuration and must follow bundler-specific naming conventions for security.\n\n```bash\n# .env\nVITE_API_URL=https://api.example.com\nVITE_ENABLE_DEVTOOLS=true\n```\n\n```typescript\n// Route configuration\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts')({\n  loader: async () => {\n    const apiUrl = import.meta.env.VITE_API_URL\n    const response = await fetch(`${apiUrl}/posts`)\n    return response.json()\n  },\n  component: PostsList,\n})\n```\n\n## Environment Variable Access Patterns\n\n### Vite-Based Projects (Most Common)\n\nWith Vite, environment variables must be prefixed with `VITE_` to be accessible in client code:\n\n```typescript\n// Route loaders\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/dashboard')({\n  loader: async () => {\n    const apiUrl = import.meta.env.VITE_API_URL        // ✅ Works\n    const apiKey = import.meta.env.VITE_PUBLIC_API_KEY // ✅ Works\n\n    // This would be undefined (security feature):\n    // const secret = import.meta.env.SECRET_KEY        // ❌ Undefined\n\n    return fetchDashboardData(apiUrl, apiKey)\n  },\n})\n\n// Components\nexport function ApiStatus() {\n  const isDev = import.meta.env.DEV           // ✅ Built-in Vite variable\n  const isProd = import.meta.env.PROD         // ✅ Built-in Vite variable\n  const mode = import.meta.env.MODE           // ✅ development/production\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      Environment: {mode}\n      {isDev && <DevToolsPanel />}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n### Webpack-Based Projects\n\nConfigure webpack's DefinePlugin to inject environment variables. **Note:** Webpack doesn't support `import.meta.env` by default, so use `process.env` patterns:\n\n```typescript\n// webpack.config.js\nconst webpack = require('webpack')\n\nmodule.exports = {\n  plugins: [\n    new webpack.DefinePlugin({\n      'process.env.API_URL': JSON.stringify(process.env.API_URL),\n      'process.env.NODE_ENV': JSON.stringify(process.env.NODE_ENV),\n      'process.env.ENABLE_FEATURE': JSON.stringify(process.env.ENABLE_FEATURE),\n    }),\n  ],\n}\n\n// Usage in routes\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/api-data')({\n  loader: async () => {\n    const response = await fetch(`${process.env.API_URL}/data`)\n    return response.json()\n  },\n  component: () => {\n    const enableFeature = process.env.ENABLE_FEATURE === 'true'\n    return enableFeature ? <NewFeature /> : <OldFeature />\n  },\n})\n```\n\n### Rspack-Based Projects\n\nRspack uses the `PUBLIC_` prefix convention. **Note:** `import.meta.env` support depends on your Rspack configuration and runtime - you may need to configure `builtins.define` properly:\n\n```bash\n# .env\nPUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.example.com\nPUBLIC_FEATURE_FLAG=true\n```\n\n```typescript\n// Route usage\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/features')({\n  loader: async () => {\n    const apiUrl = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_API_URL\n    return fetch(`${apiUrl}/features`).then(r => r.json())\n  },\n  component: () => {\n    const enableFeature = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_FEATURE_FLAG === 'true'\n    return enableFeature ? <NewFeature /> : <OldFeature />\n  },\n})\n```\n\n### ESBuild Projects\n\nConfigure defines manually:\n\n```typescript\n// build script\nimport { build } from 'esbuild'\n\nawait build({\n  entryPoints: ['src/main.tsx'],\n  define: {\n    'process.env.NODE_ENV': '\"production\"',\n    'process.env.API_URL': `\"${process.env.API_URL}\"`,\n  },\n})\n```\n\n## Common Patterns\n\n### API Configuration in Route Loaders\n\n```typescript\n// src/routes/posts/index.tsx\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nconst fetchPosts = async () => {\n  const baseUrl = import.meta.env.VITE_API_URL\n  const apiKey = import.meta.env.VITE_API_KEY\n\n  const response = await fetch(`${baseUrl}/posts`, {\n    headers: {\n      'Authorization': `Bearer ${apiKey}`,\n      'Content-Type': 'application/json',\n    },\n  })\n\n  if (!response.ok) {\n    throw new Error('Failed to fetch posts')\n  }\n\n  return response.json()\n}\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/')({\n  loader: fetchPosts,\n  errorComponent: ({ error }) => (\n    <div>Error loading posts: {error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error)}</div>\n  ),\n})\n```\n\n### Environment-Based Route Configuration\n\n```typescript\n// src/routes/__root.tsx\nimport { createRootRoute, Outlet } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport { TanStackRouterDevtools } from '@tanstack/react-router-devtools'\n\nexport const Route = createRootRoute({\n  component: () => (\n    <>\n      <Outlet />\n      {/* Only show devtools in development */}\n      {import.meta.env.DEV && <TanStackRouterDevtools />}\n    </>\n  ),\n})\n```\n\n### Feature Flags in Routes\n\n```typescript\n// src/lib/features.ts\nexport const features = {\n  enableNewDashboard: import.meta.env.VITE_ENABLE_NEW_DASHBOARD === 'true',\n  enableAnalytics: import.meta.env.VITE_ENABLE_ANALYTICS === 'true',\n  debugMode: import.meta.env.DEV,\n}\n\n// src/routes/dashboard/index.tsx\nimport { createFileRoute, redirect } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport { features } from '../../lib/features'\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/dashboard/')({\n  beforeLoad: () => {\n    // Redirect to old dashboard if new one is disabled\n    if (!features.enableNewDashboard) {\n      throw redirect({ to: '/dashboard/legacy' })\n    }\n  },\n  component: NewDashboard,\n})\n```\n\n### Authentication Configuration\n\n```typescript\n// src/lib/auth.ts\nexport const authConfig = {\n  domain: import.meta.env.VITE_AUTH0_DOMAIN,\n  clientId: import.meta.env.VITE_AUTH0_CLIENT_ID,\n  redirectUri: `${window.location.origin}/callback`,\n}\n\n// src/routes/_authenticated.tsx\nimport { createFileRoute, redirect } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport { authConfig } from '../lib/auth'\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/_authenticated')({\n  beforeLoad: async ({ location }) => {\n    const isAuthenticated = await checkAuthStatus()\n\n    if (!isAuthenticated) {\n      // Redirect to auth provider\n      const authUrl = `https://${authConfig.domain}/authorize?client_id=${authConfig.clientId}&redirect_uri=${authConfig.redirectUri}`\n      window.location.href = authUrl\n      return\n    }\n  },\n})\n```\n\n### Search Params with Environment Config\n\n```typescript\n// src/routes/search.tsx\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nconst searchSchema = z.object({\n  q: z.string().optional(),\n  category: z.string().optional(),\n})\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/search')({\n  validateSearch: searchSchema,\n  loader: async ({ search }) => {\n    const apiUrl = import.meta.env.VITE_SEARCH_API_URL\n    const params = new URLSearchParams({\n      q: search.q || '',\n      category: search.category || 'all',\n      api_key: import.meta.env.VITE_SEARCH_API_KEY,\n    })\n\n    const response = await fetch(`${apiUrl}/search?${params}`)\n    return response.json()\n  },\n})\n```\n\n## Environment File Setup\n\n### File Hierarchy (Vite)\n\nVite loads environment files in this order:\n\n```\n.env.local          # Local overrides (add to .gitignore)\n.env.production     # Production-specific\n.env.development    # Development-specific\n.env                # Default (commit to git)\n```\n\n### Example Configuration\n\n**.env** (committed to repository):\n\n```bash\n# API Configuration\nVITE_API_URL=https://api.example.com\nVITE_API_VERSION=v1\n\n# Feature Flags\nVITE_ENABLE_NEW_UI=false\nVITE_ENABLE_ANALYTICS=true\n\n# Auth Configuration (public keys only)\nVITE_AUTH0_DOMAIN=your-domain.auth0.com\nVITE_AUTH0_CLIENT_ID=your-client-id\n\n# Build Configuration\nVITE_APP_NAME=TanStack Router App\nVITE_APP_VERSION=1.0.0\n```\n\n**.env.local** (add to .gitignore):\n\n```bash\n# Development overrides\nVITE_API_URL=http://localhost:3001\nVITE_ENABLE_NEW_UI=true\nVITE_DEBUG_MODE=true\n```\n\n**.env.production**:\n\n```bash\n# Production-specific\nVITE_API_URL=https://api.prod.example.com\nVITE_ENABLE_ANALYTICS=true\nVITE_ENABLE_NEW_UI=true\n```\n\n## Type Safety\n\n### Vite TypeScript Declarations\n\nCreate `src/vite-env.d.ts`:\n\n```typescript\n/// <reference types=\"vite/client\" />\n\ninterface ImportMetaEnv {\n  // API Configuration\n  readonly VITE_API_URL: string\n  readonly VITE_API_VERSION: string\n  readonly VITE_API_KEY?: string\n\n  // Feature Flags\n  readonly VITE_ENABLE_NEW_UI: string\n  readonly VITE_ENABLE_ANALYTICS: string\n  readonly VITE_DEBUG_MODE?: string\n\n  // Authentication\n  readonly VITE_AUTH0_DOMAIN: string\n  readonly VITE_AUTH0_CLIENT_ID: string\n\n  // App Configuration\n  readonly VITE_APP_NAME: string\n  readonly VITE_APP_VERSION: string\n}\n\ninterface ImportMeta {\n  readonly env: ImportMetaEnv\n}\n```\n\n### Runtime Validation\n\nUse Zod to validate environment variables at startup with fallbacks and optional values:\n\n```typescript\n// src/config/env.ts\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nconst envSchema = z.object({\n  // Required variables\n  VITE_API_URL: z.string().url(),\n  VITE_AUTH0_DOMAIN: z.string(),\n  VITE_AUTH0_CLIENT_ID: z.string(),\n  VITE_APP_NAME: z.string(),\n\n  // Optional with defaults\n  VITE_API_VERSION: z.string().default('v1'),\n  VITE_ENABLE_NEW_UI: z.string().default('false'),\n  VITE_ENABLE_ANALYTICS: z.string().default('true'),\n\n  // Optional variables\n  VITE_DEBUG_MODE: z.string().optional(),\n  VITE_SENTRY_DSN: z.string().optional(),\n})\n\n// Validate at app startup with fallbacks\nexport const env = envSchema.parse({\n  ...import.meta.env,\n  // Provide fallbacks for missing optional values\n  VITE_API_VERSION: import.meta.env.VITE_API_VERSION || 'v1',\n  VITE_ENABLE_NEW_UI: import.meta.env.VITE_ENABLE_NEW_UI || 'false',\n  VITE_ENABLE_ANALYTICS: import.meta.env.VITE_ENABLE_ANALYTICS || 'true',\n})\n\n// Typed helper functions\nexport const isFeatureEnabled = (flag: keyof typeof env) => {\n  return env[flag] === 'true'\n}\n\n// Type-safe boolean conversion\nexport const getBooleanEnv = (\n  value: string | undefined,\n  defaultValue = false,\n): boolean => {\n  if (value === undefined) return defaultValue\n  return value === 'true'\n}\n```\n\n### Usage with Type Safety\n\n```typescript\n// src/routes/api-data.tsx\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport { env, isFeatureEnabled } from '../config/env'\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/api-data')({\n  loader: async () => {\n    // TypeScript knows these are strings and exist\n    const response = await fetch(`${env.VITE_API_URL}/${env.VITE_API_VERSION}/data`)\n    return response.json()\n  },\n  component: () => {\n    return (\n      <div>\n        <h1>{env.VITE_APP_NAME}</h1>\n        {isFeatureEnabled('VITE_ENABLE_NEW_UI') && <NewUIComponent />}\n      </div>\n    )\n  },\n})\n```\n\n## Bundler-Specific Configuration\n\n### Vite Configuration\n\n```typescript\n// vite.config.ts\nimport { defineConfig } from 'vite'\nimport react from '@vitejs/plugin-react'\nimport { tanstackRouter } from '@tanstack/router-plugin/vite'\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  plugins: [\n    react(),\n    // tanstackRouter generates route tree and enables file-based routing\n    tanstackRouter(),\n  ],\n  // Environment variables are handled automatically\n  // Custom environment variable handling:\n  define: {\n    // Global constants (these become available as global variables)\n    __APP_VERSION__: JSON.stringify(process.env.npm_package_version),\n  },\n})\n```\n\n### Webpack Configuration\n\n```typescript\n// webpack.config.js\nconst { TanStackRouterWebpack } = require('@tanstack/router-webpack-plugin')\nconst webpack = require('webpack')\n\nmodule.exports = {\n  plugins: [\n    // TanStackRouterWebpack generates route tree and enables file-based routing\n    new TanStackRouterWebpack(),\n    new webpack.DefinePlugin({\n      // Inject environment variables (use process.env for Webpack)\n      'process.env.API_URL': JSON.stringify(process.env.API_URL),\n      'process.env.NODE_ENV': JSON.stringify(process.env.NODE_ENV),\n      'process.env.ENABLE_FEATURE': JSON.stringify(process.env.ENABLE_FEATURE),\n    }),\n  ],\n}\n```\n\n### Rspack Configuration\n\n```typescript\n// rspack.config.js\nconst { TanStackRouterRspack } = require('@tanstack/router-rspack-plugin')\n\nmodule.exports = {\n  plugins: [\n    // TanStackRouterRspack generates route tree and enables file-based routing\n    new TanStackRouterRspack(),\n  ],\n  // Rspack automatically handles PUBLIC_ prefixed variables for import.meta.env\n  // Custom handling for additional variables:\n  builtins: {\n    define: {\n      // Define additional variables (these become global replacements)\n      'process.env.API_URL': JSON.stringify(process.env.PUBLIC_API_URL),\n      __BUILD_TIME__: JSON.stringify(new Date().toISOString()),\n    },\n  },\n}\n```\n\n## Production Checklist\n\n- [ ] All client-exposed variables use appropriate prefix (`VITE_`, `PUBLIC_`, etc.)\n- [ ] No sensitive data (API secrets, private keys) in environment variables\n- [ ] `.env.local` is in `.gitignore`\n- [ ] Production environment variables are configured on hosting platform\n- [ ] Required environment variables are validated at build time\n- [ ] TypeScript declarations are up to date\n- [ ] Feature flags are properly configured for production\n- [ ] API URLs point to production endpoints\n\n## Common Problems\n\n### Environment Variable is Undefined\n\n**Problem**: `import.meta.env.MY_VARIABLE` returns `undefined`\n\n**Solutions**:\n\n1. **Add correct prefix**: Use `VITE_` for Vite, `PUBLIC_` for Rspack.\n   Vite's default prefix may be changed in the config:\n   ```ts\n   // vite.config.ts\n   export const config = {\n     // ...rest of your config\n     envPrefix: 'MYPREFIX_', // this means `MYPREFIX_MY_VARIABLE` is the new correct way\n   }\n   ```\n2. **Restart development server** after adding new variables\n3. **Check file location**: `.env` file must be in project root\n4. **Verify bundler configuration**: Ensure variables are properly injected\n5. **Verify variable**:\n\n- **In dev**: is in correct `.env` file or environment\n- **For prod**: is in correct `.env` file or current environment **_at bundle time_**. That's right, `VITE_`/`PUBLIC_`-prefixed variables are replaced in a macro-like fashion at bundle time, and will _never_ be read at runtime on your server. This is a common mistake, so make sure this is not your case.\n\n**Example**:\n\n```bash\n# ❌ Won't work (no prefix)\nAPI_KEY=abc123\n\n# ✅ Works with Vite\nVITE_API_KEY=abc123\n\n# ✅ Works with Rspack\nPUBLIC_API_KEY=abc123\n\n# ❌ Won't bundle the variable (assuming it is not set in the environment of the build)\nnpm run build\n\n# ✅ Works with Vite and will bundle the variable for production\nVITE_API_KEY=abc123 npm run build\n\n# ✅ Works with Rspack and will bundle the variable for production\nPUBLIC_API_KEY=abc123 npm run build\n```\n\n### Runtime Client Environment Variables at Runtime in Production\n\n**Problem**: If `VITE_`/`PUBLIC_` variables are replaced at bundle time only, how to make runtime variables available on the client ?\n\n**Solutions**:\n\nPass variables from the server down to the client:\n\n1. Add your variable to the correct `env.` file\n2. Create an endpoint on your server to read the value from the client\n\n**Example**:\n\nYou may use your prefered backend framework/libray, but here it is using Tanstack Start server functions:\n\n```tsx\nconst getRuntimeVar = createServerFn({ method: 'GET' }).handler(() => {\n  return process.env.MY_RUNTIME_VAR // notice `process.env` on the server, and no `VITE_`/`PUBLIC_` prefix\n})\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/')({\n  loader: async () => {\n    const foo = await getRuntimeVar()\n    return { foo }\n  },\n  component: RouteComponent,\n})\n\nfunction RouteComponent() {\n  const { foo } = Route.useLoaderData()\n  // ... use your variable however you want\n}\n```\n\n### Variable Not Updating\n\n**Problem**: Environment variable changes aren't reflected in app\n\n**Solutions**:\n\n1. **Restart development server** - Required for new variables\n2. **Check file hierarchy** - `.env.local` overrides `.env`\n3. **Clear browser cache** - Hard refresh (Ctrl+Shift+R)\n4. **Verify correct file** - Make sure you're editing the right `.env` file\n\n### TypeScript Errors\n\n**Problem**: `Property 'VITE_MY_VAR' does not exist on type 'ImportMetaEnv'`\n\n**Solution**: Add declaration to `src/vite-env.d.ts`:\n\n```typescript\ninterface ImportMetaEnv {\n  readonly VITE_MY_VAR: string\n}\n```\n\n### Build Errors\n\n**Problem**: Missing environment variables during build\n\n**Solutions**:\n\n1. **Configure CI/CD**: Set variables in build environment\n2. **Add validation**: Check required variables at build time\n3. **Use .env files**: Ensure production `.env` files exist\n4. **Check bundler config**: Verify environment variable injection\n\n### Security Issues\n\n**Problem**: Accidentally exposing sensitive data\n\n**Solutions**:\n\n1. **Never use secrets in client variables** - They're visible in browser\n2. **Use server-side proxies** for sensitive API calls\n3. **Audit bundle** - Check built files for leaked secrets\n4. **Follow naming conventions** - Only prefixed variables are exposed\n\n### Runtime vs Build-time Confusion\n\n**Problem**: Variables not available at runtime\n\n**Solutions**:\n\n1. **Understand static replacement** - Variables are replaced at build time\n2. **Use server-side for dynamic values** - Use APIs for runtime configuration\n3. **Validate at startup** - Check all required variables exist\n\n### Environment Variables are Always Strings\n\n**Problem**: Unexpected behavior when comparing boolean or numeric values\n\n**Solutions**:\n\n1. **Always compare as strings**: Use `=== 'true'` not `=== true`\n2. **Convert explicitly**: Use `parseInt()`, `parseFloat()`, or `Boolean()`\n3. **Use helper functions**: Create typed conversion utilities\n\n**Example**:\n\n```typescript\n// ❌ Won't work as expected\nconst isEnabled = import.meta.env.VITE_FEATURE_ENABLED // This is a string!\nif (isEnabled) {\n  /* Always true if variable exists */\n}\n\n// ✅ Correct string comparison\nconst isEnabled = import.meta.env.VITE_FEATURE_ENABLED === 'true'\n\n// ✅ Safe numeric conversion\nconst port = parseInt(import.meta.env.VITE_PORT || '3000', 10)\n\n// ✅ Helper function approach\nconst getBooleanEnv = (value: string | undefined, defaultValue = false) => {\n  if (value === undefined) return defaultValue\n  return value.toLowerCase() === 'true'\n}\n```\n\n## Common Next Steps\n\n<!-- [Set Up Authentication](./setup-authentication.md) - Configure auth providers with environment variables -->\n<!-- [Deploy to Production](./deploy-to-production.md) - Set up production environment variables -->\n<!-- [Set Up API Integration](./setup-api-integration.md) - Configure API endpoints and keys -->\n\n## Related Resources\n\n- [TanStack Router File-Based Routing](../routing/file-based-routing.md) - Learn about route configuration\n- [Vite Environment Variables](https://vitejs.dev/guide/env-and-mode.html) - Official Vite documentation\n- [Webpack DefinePlugin](https://webpack.js.org/plugins/define-plugin/) - Webpack environment configuration\n"}
